  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Community-Led Recovery and Resilience through the sclr Approach in Lebanon</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This intervention aims to support community-led recovery in two conflict-affected areas of Lebanon&#x2019;s Beqaa region: Sohmour in West Beqaa, which was directly targeted during the recent conflict, and Bar Elias in Central Beqaa, which has absorbed a large number of internally displaced persons (IDPs). Both areas suffer from critical service disruptions and poor infrastructure, leaving communities with needs and limited support mechanisms. 
The project supports communities through the implementation of at least 15 small-scale community-led initiatives, using the support to Community-Led Response (SCLR) approach. These initiatives will be led by informal community groups (initiatives) and inclusive community committees.</narrative>
  </description>
